# Project excludes
docs/_examples
sg_execution_times.rst
/results/*
!/results/fg1_golden_main.json
!/results/fg1_physics_parity.json
*.npz
*.ipynb

# FG-2 acceptance artifacts are committed so every F2-1..F2-8 number can be
# recomputed from a tracked product (cross-WP rule 2). Placed after *.npz so the
# negation takes effect.
!/results/fg2_evidence.json
!/results/fg2_golden_cplusl_230x50.npz

# FG-4a acceptance artifacts are committed for the same reason: the golden is
# the gate every later optimisation must pass, and the timings are the only
# source for the speedup numbers, so both must be recomputable from a tracked
# product rather than from prose.
!/results/fg4a_golden.json
!/results/fg4a_bench_baseline.json
!/results/fg4a_bench_fg4a.json
!/results/fg4a_bench_fg4a_vs_baseline.json
!/results/fg4a_speedup_ab.json
!/results/fg4b_speedup_ab.json

# FG-U1 acceptance artifact, same rationale: every legacy-vs-tabular number in
# docs/fg-u1_raman_spectrum.md (tilt, per-channel SNR deltas, interpolation
# error, asymmetry magnitudes) must be recomputable from a tracked product
# rather than from prose.
!/results/fg_u1_raman.json

# FU-2 acceptance artifact, same rationale: every number in
# docs/fu2_scu_evaluation.md (band edges, guards, span report, N / bandwidth /
# occupancy, per-band launch power, per-channel SNR, Raman tilt, legacy-vs-tabular
# deltas, and the U/L gap ablation) must be recomputable from a tracked product
# rather than from prose. Regenerate with
# scripts/fu2_scu_evidence.py; verify with the same script's --check.
!/results/fg_u2_scu.json

# FG-4e acceptance artifacts: the batch-vs-serial speedup curve and the
# per-candidate numeric check are the only source for the B=68 speedup, so they
# are committed twice on purpose -- the two runs are independent samples and the
# run-to-run spread is part of the reported result (see docs/fg4e_cpu_batching.md §4.2).
!/results/fg4e_speedup_ab.json
!/results/fg4e_speedup_ab_run2.json

# FG-4g attribution artifact: the verdict that the 0.314 dB scan-vs-gate split
# is a baseline skew and NOT an ode_accel effect rests entirely on the tier
# invariance recorded here. docs/fg4g_matvec_attribution.md is rendered from it
# and re-renderable via `scripts/fg4g_render_doc.py --check`, so the JSON has to
# be tracked for the document to be verifiable rather than merely assertable.
!/results/fg4g_attribution.json

# FG-5 integration artifact: the post-merge ΔSNR table and the four re-run gate
# results. docs/fg5_integration_note.md is rendered from it and re-renderable via
# `scripts/fg5_integration_evidence.py --check`, tracked for the same reason.
!/results/fg5_integration.json

# FG-13 adjudication artifacts, same rationale: every number in
# docs/fg13_evaluate_path_roadm.md -- the field-liveness census (which ROADM
# fields are inert on evaluate_path, and by how much), the last-hop vs non-last-hop
# structural control, and the per-scenario dBSNR impact of switching to the
# authoritative assembly -- must be recomputable from a tracked product rather
# than from prose. `fg13_roadm_probe.json` is re-verifiable with
# `scripts/fg13_probe_roadm.py --check`; `fg13_impact_probe.json` is regenerated
# by `scripts/fg13_impact_probe.py`.
!/results/fg13_roadm_probe.json
!/results/fg13_impact_probe.json
